  "rules": [
    "Use one primary category path per canonical product; additional navigation tags do not create duplicate products.",
    "Use only approved IDs. Assign the deepest supported level; leave unknown levels null. Empty product_types arrays are reserved for future approval, not permission to invent types.",
    "Classify using verified product identity, composition, intended use and official documentation; supplier category is evidence, not authoritative truth. Preserve original supplier labels and source URLs.",
    "For overlaps prefer the specific verified product type: hair-specific mesotherapy goes to Hair Mesotherapy; botulinum toxins go to C02 even when prescription-only; hyaluronidase goes to C08. For unresolved overlaps use REVIEW_REQUIRED.",
    "Treatment area (Lip, Face, Body) is a facet, not a primary category. Mono, Cog and Screw are thread design facets; PDO, PLLA and PCL are material categories.",
    "Brand, manufacturer, dose, strength, volume, pack size, route, regulatory status, prescription requirements and professional eligibility are independent attributes. Never infer legal status from category.",
    "Do not automatically overwrite canonical Product Truth with supplier data. Manufacturer or official documentation takes precedence. Keep field-level source, confidence and audit history.",
    "Distinguish MANUFACTURER_STANDARD, SUPPLIER_SPLIT, SUPPLIER_BUNDLE and UNKNOWN. Require evidence or supplier confirmation for custom/split packs. Do not merge different variants or packs as identical offers.",
    "Exclude unresolved or conflicting offers from automated cheapest and basket recommendations. Route conflicts to verification queue.",
    "Do not force a classification or invent evidence. Preserve unmatched records and propose new categories separately for human approval.",
    "Taxonomy includes future scope; inclusion does not imply supplier availability, UK authorisation or permission to sell.",
    "Best Sellers, New Arrivals and Special Offers are collections; Training and Marketing are services, not product categories."
  ],
